{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide node2 SNMPv2c read access to node1 using community branch-readonly, exposing system identity, uptime, sysLocation \"West Branch\", and sysContact \"ops@branch.test\".","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"A live query from node2 successfully returned node1 identity, uptime, contact, hostname, and location. The service was active, enabled, listening on UDP/161, and firewalled to node2. However, both configuration and test commands reference the concealed SNMP_COMMUNITY variable, so the captured evidence does not establish that its value was exactly branch-readonly.","evidence_ids":["cmd-01b04b17b38e49df","cmd-de8832f43f75423e","cmd-9129fb0d63e24825"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Permit reads through the community while rejecting writes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The same credentials successfully read system OIDs. An attempted sysLocation write failed with noAccess and return code 2, and a subsequent read confirmed that the value remained \"West Branch\".","evidence_ids":["cmd-9129fb0d63e24825"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the asset register under /srv/legacy2/snmp-readonly-monitoring.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The register retained its baseline SHA-256 hash, size, ownership, mode, timestamp, and content on both nodes immediately before implementation. The complete subsequent command timeline contains no operation targeting that directory or file.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-b6c1a6d0dd684e73","cmd-ee0254e29bb84a40"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 9.8 with kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8. The executor installed RHEL 9 net-snmp 5.9.1 packages from the enabled Red Hat repositories, with no command upgrading the OS or kernel.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","cmd-aa72b4bc60bb40c3","cmd-a1b11bdb80694922","cmd-3e6372a32b3c4175","cmd-5a9076e806ee46e4"]}],"confidence":0.76,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing the SNMP agent and client packages was necessary; replacing the agent configuration and retaining a distribution backup supported implementation and recovery; adding the source-restricted firewall rule and enabling the service provided the required access; and the rejected SNMP SET was a bounded verification attempt that left sysLocation unchanged. Final hygiene inspection was prevented by lease expiry, so failed-service, package-health, temporary-file, and residue state could not be independently confirmed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3e6372a32b3c4175","cmd-5a9076e806ee46e4","cmd-01b04b17b38e49df","cmd-de8832f43f75423e","cmd-9129fb0d63e24825","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The observable SNMP behavior, read-only enforcement, asset preservation, and platform compatibility were achieved. The only task-specific evidentiary gap is that the exact community string was redacted behind an environment variable. The mandatory provider-wide restart protocol was not performed before the cluster lease expired, substantially limiting evidence of persistence but not directly reducing task functionality because restart behavior was not part of the public contract.","limitations":["The captured commands never reveal the value of SNMP_COMMUNITY, so exact use of branch-readonly cannot be verified.","No provider-wide node-restart evidence was collected for either node: there are no pre-restart health records tied to a restart, restart acknowledgements, changed post-restart boot identities, or recovered service/data state.","The fixed after-prepare boot identities were 98aa35f5-6905-42fd-9f07-0e28f75b4fa6 on node1 and fbdf5b2c-bb43-49f6-935d-fb98f8a972f6 on node2, but all after-executor boot observations were unavailable because the cluster lease expired.","Lease expiry also prevented an independent final snapshot of service health, package consistency, listening sockets, temporary files, platform state, and asset state."]}
